            <div xml:id="d683">

                <pb facs="0617" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.20/493</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4911</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-08-31">August 31, 1939</date>.<lb/>[Received September
                        19.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my telegram
                    No. 1658 of August 29, 7 p.m.,<anchor n="48" xml:id="d683-f1"/> and to enclose
                    herewith, with English translation, a copy of a note addressed by the French
                    Foreign Office, under date of August 26, 1939, to the Liberian Legation in
                    Paris.</p>
                <p>In furnishing me with a copy of this note, the Liberian Minister expressed his
                    deepest personal thanks and the gratitude of the Liberian Government for the
                    assistance given in this matter by this Mission.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William C.
                    Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d683-a1.xml" xpointer="d683-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
